      "en": "**sarcasm** = saying the opposite of what you mean in a mocking tone («Great, another outage»), and **irony** = a contrast between what is expected and what happens. In writing, sarcasm is easily misunderstood — avoid it with clients. **subtext** = the unwritten message. If unsure, ask politely: «Just to make sure I understand — would you prefer…?»"
